From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: build TinyUSB 0.21 (MicroPython's own tag).

The esp32 port builds TinyUSB from the espressif/tinyusb managed
component, pinned to micropython/tinyusb-espressif's
cherrypick/dwc2_zlp_fix branch: TinyUSB 0.18 plus the DWC2 OUT-endpoint
ZLP fix (hathach/tinyusb#3154, fixed by #3293). This keeps that source
and moves every target that builds TinyUSB (S2, S3, P4) to
v0.21.0.1-micropython1, MicroPython's own tag in the same fork.

That tag is espressif/tinyusb 0.21.0~1 plus Damien George's "don't
flush pending data in cdcd_open" (hathach/tinyusb#3807, merged upstream
as #3808). It carries the ZLP fix ("short packet (including ZLP when
byte_count == 0)" in dcd_dwc2.c). Against the registry's 0.21.0~2 it
lacks only a DWC2 periodic-transfer option that is off by default and
an NCM divisor change, neither of which this port uses.

It has to be that tag and not a plain 0.21 release. On a LILYGO T-Embed
(ESP32-S3, full speed) espressif's 0.21.0~1 and ~2 enumerate, but the
moment the host opens the CDC port with DTR raised the chip trips the
interrupt watchdog inside the DWC2 IN-endpoint handler
(dcd_int_handler -> handle_ep_irq, dir IN) and reboots. With
CFG_TUD_CDC_TX_PERSISTENT, which MicroPython sets, their cdcd_open()
starts a transfer from the persistent TX FIFO during enumeration. The
tag's one extra commit removes that, and on the tag the S3 opens its
port and runs normally (usbif#48).

What this changes for a USB audio device: from 0.19 the audio class
finishes an isochronous OUT packet in the USB interrupt
(audiod_xfer_isr): it copies the packet into the endpoint FIFO, re-arms
the endpoint and calls tud_audio_rx_done_isr(). In 0.18 all of that
waited for tud_task(), which on this port runs in the MicroPython task
through the scheduler, so a busy interpreter left the endpoint unarmed
and lost packets. Measured on usbif sound cards with the interpreter
allocating in a tight loop: 91-95 % of packets delivered on an ESP32-P4
and 87-94 % on an ESP32-S3 on 0.18, heard as a tick every few tens of
milliseconds; 100 % on both with this tag.

The API changes that reach a user C module are 0.19's and 0.20's:
tud_audio_rx_done_post_read_cb() became tud_audio_rx_done_isr() and
runs in the ISR, and TUD_AUDIO_EP_SIZE() takes the bus speed as its
first argument. Nothing in MicroPython itself uses either.

One behaviour change to know about: 0.21's DWC2 driver arms an
isochronous OUT endpoint for the microframe after the current one,
whatever its interval (0.18 did that only for bInterval 1). A
high-speed isochronous OUT endpoint with a longer interval then waits
on the wrong frame parity and receives nothing; usbif's sound card at
bInterval 4 got no packets at all until it went back to 1, which the
interrupt-time re-arm makes safe.

The S2, S3 and P4 lockfiles are part of this patch, and only their
TinyUSB entries move, to the tag's commit. The component manager
re-solves when the manifest changes, but it keeps a git commit it has
already locked for as long as the source is the same, and here the
source is. Without the lockfile change a target would quietly go on
building 0.18.
---
diff --git a/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32p4 b/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32p4
index a338b20..cc6e557 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32p4
+++ b/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32p4
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ dependencies:
       type: service
     version: 1.3.2
   espressif/tinyusb:
-    component_hash: ee1c962cff61eb975d508258d509974d58031cc27ff0d6c4117a67a613a49594
+    component_hash: b8cf4577c72e77dcc180f2fd46fe6ea9883190e389c5fe90504a47908ae02637
     dependencies:
     - name: idf
       version: '>=5.0'
@@ -77,7 +77,8 @@ dependencies:
     - esp32s3
     - esp32p4
     - esp32h4
-    version: e4c0ec3caab3d9c25374de7047653b9ced8f14ff
+    - esp32s31
+    version: 5c5c660317943820d49ce5c188f1bd60cd8aade6
   idf:
     source:
       type: idf
diff --git a/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32s2 b/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32s2
index ba79ccc..65b20d0 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32s2
+++ b/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32s2
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ dependencies:
       type: service
     version: 1.3.2
   espressif/tinyusb:
-    component_hash: ee1c962cff61eb975d508258d509974d58031cc27ff0d6c4117a67a613a49594
+    component_hash: b8cf4577c72e77dcc180f2fd46fe6ea9883190e389c5fe90504a47908ae02637
     dependencies:
     - name: idf
       version: '>=5.0'
@@ -23,7 +23,8 @@ dependencies:
     - esp32s3
     - esp32p4
     - esp32h4
-    version: e4c0ec3caab3d9c25374de7047653b9ced8f14ff
+    - esp32s31
+    version: 5c5c660317943820d49ce5c188f1bd60cd8aade6
   idf:
     source:
       type: idf
diff --git a/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32s3 b/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32s3
index a57ac9a..7bc077a 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32s3
+++ b/ports/esp32/lockfiles/dependencies.lock.esp32s3
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ dependencies:
       type: service
     version: 1.3.2
   espressif/tinyusb:
-    component_hash: ee1c962cff61eb975d508258d509974d58031cc27ff0d6c4117a67a613a49594
+    component_hash: b8cf4577c72e77dcc180f2fd46fe6ea9883190e389c5fe90504a47908ae02637
     dependencies:
     - name: idf
       version: '>=5.0'
@@ -23,7 +23,8 @@ dependencies:
     - esp32s3
     - esp32p4
     - esp32h4
-    version: e4c0ec3caab3d9c25374de7047653b9ced8f14ff
+    - esp32s31
+    version: 5c5c660317943820d49ce5c188f1bd60cd8aade6
   idf:
     source:
       type: idf
diff --git a/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml b/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml
index ddd7cb2..3c352a8 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml
+++ b/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml
@@ -5,10 +5,14 @@ dependencies:
   espressif/tinyusb:
     rules:
       - if: "target in [esp32s2, esp32s3, esp32p4]"
-    # Temporary workaround for https://github.com/hathach/tinyusb/issues/3154
-    # Can be removed once fix is released in espressif/tinyusb
+    # TinyUSB 0.21, MicroPython's own tag: espressif/tinyusb 0.21.0~1 plus
+    # the cdcd_open fix (hathach/tinyusb#3808). It carries the OUT-endpoint
+    # ZLP fix (#3293) the cherrypick/dwc2_zlp_fix branch was holding, and it
+    # re-arms the audio class's isochronous OUT endpoint in the ISR, not in
+    # tud_task(). Without #3808 an ESP32-S3 resets when the host opens the
+    # CDC port, which is why this is the tag and not the registry's 0.21.0~2.
     git: https://github.com/micropython/tinyusb-espressif.git
-    version: cherrypick/dwc2_zlp_fix
+    version: v0.21.0.1-micropython1
   espressif/esp_hosted:
     rules:
       - if: "target == esp32p4"
